From d29b0f809cb1afc39bfd97db2f1fa118d10f5422 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:08:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm/mt7981: eMMC boot flash (MSDC host, flash=emmc)

MT7986 routers such as the GL.iNet GL-MT6000 boot from eMMC: BL2 in boot
partition 0, FIP, kernel and rootfs in GPT partitions of the user area.

- mt7981_msdc.c: MediaTek MSDC SD/MMC host (mtk-sd) at 0x11230000, SPI
  143, with the card on a QEMU SD bus.  Commands with R1/R1b/R2/R3
  responses, auto CMD23 / CMD12, PIO through the FIFO (TF-A, U-Boot) and
  GPD/BD descriptor DMA (Linux); tuning/sampling registers are storage.
- machine option flash=emmc: a QEMU eMMC (TYPE_EMMC) with two boot
  partitions of emmc-boot MB (default 4) in front of the user area, from
  -drive if=sd or the first *.img file of the flash folder.
- BootROM: "EMMC_BOOT" header + BRLYT in boot partition 0, BL2 GFH found
  on a 512-byte boundary.
- gmac0-phy-addr / gmac1-phy-addr: MDIO address of a 2.5G PHY on a GMAC
  (the GL-MT6000 has its WAN PHY at address 1).

Tested with the official OpenWrt 25.12.5 images of the GL-MT6000: BL2
finds the FIP by GPT name, U-Boot boots the kernel partition, Linux sees
mmcblk0 with its partitions and boot0/boot1, mounts the rootfs and the
f2fs overlay; settings survive a reboot.
